  "description": "Small open-hardware analogue front-end (AFE) board for acquiring biopotential signals — ECG, EMG, EEG, and EOG — from the body for use with microcontrollers such as Arduino. Widely used in education, maker, and research biosignal projects; full schematics, PCB, and example firmware are published.",
